    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 81. क्वचित्—may better be taken as an adv. of time; at one",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "time, at another, भूमीशायी is a better reading than भूमौ शायी as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "keeping up symmetry. शाल्योदन०—Having a liking for S'áli ( a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "superior kind of paddy ) only. कन्थाधारी—One wearing a wallet.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "मनस्वी—from मनस् + विनिः high-souled, also wise. विन् shows",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "प्राशस्त्य. कार्यार्थी ( कार्यं अर्थयते इति ) One that seeks to gain",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "his object. This as well as कन्थाधारी and शाकाहारी are formed by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "affixing इन् ( णिनिः ) by सुप्यजातौ णिनिस्ताच्छील्ये ( इन् is added",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "to a root in the sense of ‘in the habit of’ when it is preceded",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "by a noun not denoting a class ). कार्यार्थी may also betaken",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "as in the com.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 82. उपशम—Subduing the passions, tranquillity. प्रभवितृ–",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "One possessing absolute power. This is the only concrete noun",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "used in the sloka for प्रभावस्य. निर्व्याजता—freedom from hypoc-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "risy. सर्वेषाम् &c.—Some take this to mean ‘of all persons,’ in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "which sense अपि would be superfluous. सर्वकारणम् cause of all",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "i. e. of ऐश्वर्य, सुजनता &c. शील–virtuous or good conduct.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 83. नीति—The condut of human affairs, rules of life. यदि",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "वा—is equivalent here to अथवा. न्याय्यात्–see sl. 28. supra.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "धीराः—धियं बुद्धिमीरयन्ति सर्वतः प्रवर्तयन्तीति । Ràmarshi. The wise.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 84. कदर्थितस्य-p. p. of कदर्थय् denom. fr. कदर्थ ( कुत्सितोर्थः )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of one who is despised, afflicted, worried. प्रमार्ष्टुम्—to wipe off",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "completely, to obliterate. Mr. Telang rightly remarks that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "अधोमुखस्य कृतस्य is not a usual construction and that therefore",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the reading तनूनपातः ( see foot-note p. 34 ) is better. This, how-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "ever, is open to another objection; for it involves the दोष—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "अप्रयुक्तत्व, the word तनूनपात्—though given by the lexicogra-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "phers for ‘fire, being hardly, if ever, used by the poets. The fig.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "is दृष्टान्त.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 85. न लुनन्ति ‘cut or wound’, or pierce. कटाक्षविशिखाः—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "arrows in the form of glances. कृशानुः-कृशयति that which reduces",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "size; hence fire; कृश्+आनु ( क ). Construe यस्य चित्तं कान्ता० न",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "खनन्ति ०तापः न दहति and so on.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
